Role: code and test editor. Match each file's existing style. Comments state the durable reason only: no review ids, spec paths or phase numbers.

Problem: four copies of the OpenCode version-output classifier exist, and nothing keeps them in step:
- `parseOpencodeVersion` in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/opencode-version.mjs` (the reference; the dispatch guard uses it)
- `parseOpencodeVersion` in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/opencode-version.cjs` (exported via module.exports)
- `parseVersion` in `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/opencode-version-battery.cjs` (exported)
- `classify_version` in `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/scripts/opencode-setup.sh`, which reads a narrower grammar: v1 only as a bare `1.x.y` line, and v2 only as `opencode 2.x.y`.

Fix with one shared fixture corpus that every copy is tested against. Do not merge the copies into one module.

1. Create `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/opencode-version-corpus.json`: a JSON array of `{ "output": "<probe output>", "family": "v1" | "v2" | "unknown" }`. Include at least: `1.19.3`, `v1.19.3`, `opencode 1.19.3`, `1.19.3-beta.1`, `2.0.32`, `opencode 2.0.32`, `opencode v2.0.32`, `3.0.0`, `0.9.1`, `not a version`, an empty string, and a two-line output whose first line is a warning and whose second line is `1.19.3`. Set each `family` to what the reference `parseOpencodeVersion` in the .mjs actually returns. Run it with node to get the values, and do not guess.
2. Change `classify_version` in `opencode-setup.sh` to the reference grammar. Per line, check each whitespace-separated token against `^[vV]?([0-9]+)\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+([-+][^[:space:]]*)?$`. The first matching token decides: major 1 prints v1, major 2 prints v2, any other major prints unknown. With no match on any line it prints unknown. Keep the function's name, its stdin input and its single printed word.
3. Tests that read the corpus and assert every entry:
   - in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs` for the .mjs parser;
   - in `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/opencode-version-battery.test.cjs` for `parseVersion`;
   - in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/unit/opencode-dual-dispatch.vitest.ts` for the .cjs `parseOpencodeVersion`; read how that file already imports the script;
   - a new `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/scripts/tests/opencode-setup-classify.test.cjs` (node:test) that extracts `classify_version` with `sed -n '/^classify_version()/,/^}/p'`, then for each entry runs `bash -c` with that function defined, pipes the output in with printf, and compares the result.

Checks, using node from `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v26.8.2/bin`:
- `node --test .skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/opencode-version-battery.test.cjs .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/scripts/tests/opencode-setup-classify.test.cjs`
- `cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime && npx vitest run --no-coverage tests/unit/opencode-dual-dispatch.vitest.ts`
- `bash -n .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/scripts/opencode-setup.sh`
Report every pass and fail count, and the corpus you wrote. Edit no other file.
